# Known bug: a permanent's play rules (no maximum hand size, extra land plays, ...) are read off its card whether or not it has lost all its abilities (CR 613.1f, 402.2); `no_maximum_hand_size` and `land_rules` in actions.rs never look at LoseAllAbilities.
# Bot2's The Wondrous Wasp strips Ms. Marvel of every ability on turn 2, her "You have no maximum hand size" with them. On turn 3
# Bot1 draws up to eight cards with two Ancestral Recalls and, having no such ability, must discard one at cleanup (CR 514.1).
# (ms-marvel-gives-no-maximum-hand-size is the positive control: the same turn without the Wasp discards nothing.)

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Ms. Marvel, Kamala Khan
Ancestral Recall
Ancestral Recall
Ancestral Recall
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
The Wondrous Wasp
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ms. Marvel, Kamala Khan.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.The Wondrous Wasp.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Target(Ms. Marvel, Kamala Khan)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ms. Marvel, Kamala Khan.Keywords = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ancestral Recall.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ancestral Recall.Cast(Bot1)
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Discard(Island)

[Expect]
Bot1.Hand.Count = 7
